1
00:00:05,095 --> 00:00:06,346
By the way...

2
00:00:08,432 --> 00:00:11,643
I told him. I told Taiki that I like him.

3
00:00:14,062 --> 00:00:15,105
[gasps softly]

4
00:00:16,398 --> 00:00:18,316
[wind blowing]

5
00:00:22,404 --> 00:00:23,321
Oh, gotcha.

6
00:00:23,405 --> 00:00:25,824
[grunts hesitantly] Uh, so...

7
00:00:25,907 --> 00:00:29,077
I mean, since the two of you
are living together,

8
00:00:29,161 --> 00:00:31,580
I thought I should give you
a heads-up, right?

9
00:00:31,663 --> 00:00:34,833
But I don't want you to treat me
differently or anything.

10
00:00:34,916 --> 00:00:37,127
Actually, for the time being,

11
00:00:37,210 --> 00:00:39,379
I'm not staying with Taiki and his family.

12
00:00:39,463 --> 00:00:40,714
Uh?

13
00:00:40,797 --> 00:00:43,049
My grandfather has to have surgery.

14
00:00:44,551 --> 00:00:47,888
That's why my mom's back
in Japan for a while.

15
00:00:47,971 --> 00:00:51,433
I'm gonna stay with her until
my grandfather's procedure in a month.

16
00:00:54,019 --> 00:00:55,854
[exclaims in surprise]

17
00:00:58,899 --> 00:01:00,108
Oh, I didn't know!

18
00:01:00,192 --> 00:01:03,612
I hope his surgery goes smoothly
and there aren't any issues.

19
00:01:04,362 --> 00:01:07,032
I'll go and take care
of some other things now,

20
00:01:07,115 --> 00:01:09,493
so please take your time
with the copy machine!

21
00:01:10,702 --> 00:01:11,995
See you.

22
00:01:14,331 --> 00:01:15,832
[door sliding]

23
00:01:21,379 --> 00:01:22,631
[machine whirring]

24
00:01:35,852 --> 00:01:37,854
[opening theme song playing]

25
00:02:02,212 --> 00:02:05,632
BLUE BOX

26
00:03:05,525 --> 00:03:08,987
EPISODE 17
OF COURSE I WANT TO SEE IT

27
00:03:16,995 --> 00:03:19,247
[both] Thank you for the practice match.

28
00:03:21,917 --> 00:03:24,753
[boy] Taiki!
You've stepped it up recently.

29
00:03:25,503 --> 00:03:29,257
You look more relaxed on the court,
and your movement's less rigid.

30
00:03:30,926 --> 00:03:32,302
Thanks for saying that.

31
00:03:35,013 --> 00:03:36,264
<i>I don't know.</i>

32
00:03:36,348 --> 00:03:38,892
<i>I don't feel like any of that's true.</i>

33
00:03:39,684 --> 00:03:42,187
<i>I can score more points than I used to,</i>

34
00:03:42,729 --> 00:03:44,606
<i>and my movement on the court is better.</i>

35
00:03:45,857 --> 00:03:46,983
<i>So then...</i>

36
00:03:47,984 --> 00:03:49,903
<i>why am I feeling so...</i>

37
00:03:50,779 --> 00:03:51,988
<i>stuck.</i>

38
00:03:54,824 --> 00:03:55,992
[Coach Yuasa] Gather 'round!

39
00:03:58,245 --> 00:04:02,290
Scheduling one's been tricky, but we now
have a practice match on Saturday.

40
00:04:03,375 --> 00:04:04,918
Who are we up against?

41
00:04:05,001 --> 00:04:06,795
[Coach Yuasa] Hold on, hold on.

42
00:04:07,587 --> 00:04:10,090
{\an8}We'll be playing Sajikawa High School.

43
00:04:10,173 --> 00:04:11,800
{\an8}SAJIKAWA

44
00:04:11,883 --> 00:04:13,301
[gasps softly]

45
00:04:13,385 --> 00:04:14,511
[♪ mellow music playing]

46
00:04:18,139 --> 00:04:21,184
- [Taiki] A rematch?
- [boy 1] Really? Heck yeah!

47
00:04:21,268 --> 00:04:23,895
[boy 2] We won't get to play
against Hyodo though.

48
00:04:23,979 --> 00:04:27,565
Even without the third-years,
that team has a lotta talent.

49
00:04:27,649 --> 00:04:29,192
For next year's nationals,

50
00:04:29,276 --> 00:04:31,903
Sajikawa is our biggest obstacle
to overcome.

51
00:04:31,987 --> 00:04:32,821
[all] Yes, sir!

52
00:04:32,904 --> 00:04:34,447
This is great timing.

53
00:04:35,156 --> 00:04:37,951
I was hoping to go up
against that first-year.

54
00:04:38,034 --> 00:04:40,870
- [boy] Who, Yusa?
- Yeah, the one whose face says,

55
00:04:40,954 --> 00:04:43,832
"I wear turtlenecks in the winter." Uh...

56
00:04:43,915 --> 00:04:45,834
[boy] What kind of a face is that?

57
00:04:48,420 --> 00:04:50,338
Okay, what's up with this nervous act.

58
00:04:51,172 --> 00:04:54,926
You've lost to the guy already,
just give it your best shot.

59
00:04:55,010 --> 00:04:57,762
[boy] Not much of a pep talk, Haryu.

60
00:04:57,846 --> 00:04:59,222
[Taiki] I'll do my best.

61
00:05:04,644 --> 00:05:06,354
[Hina] So, word on the street is...

62
00:05:06,438 --> 00:05:07,856
{\an8}SNOW WHITE

63
00:05:07,939 --> 00:05:10,608
...you have a practice match on Saturday.

64
00:05:10,692 --> 00:05:13,862
[Taiki] You can run, read your script,
or talk, but pick one.

65
00:05:13,945 --> 00:05:16,364
But it's more efficient this way.

66
00:05:16,448 --> 00:05:19,826
They say that exercise
helps you memorize things better.

67
00:05:19,909 --> 00:05:21,369
You can do it all, can't you?

68
00:05:21,453 --> 00:05:25,999
I don't have gymnastics Saturday,
but I'm gonna be here for rehearsal,

69
00:05:26,082 --> 00:05:28,251
so I can come cheer you on
while you're playing.

70
00:05:28,334 --> 00:05:29,878
- It's okay.
- Huh?

71
00:05:30,712 --> 00:05:32,756
[Taiki] It's only a practice match.

72
00:05:32,839 --> 00:05:35,508
[Hina] But you're facing
a rival school, right?

73
00:05:35,592 --> 00:05:36,968
[Taiki] Yeah, we are, but...

74
00:05:37,052 --> 00:05:39,554
Wasn't the match
you lost before to this team?

75
00:05:39,637 --> 00:05:42,390
[Taiki] <i>Oh, right,
Hina was there that day.</i>

76
00:05:43,433 --> 00:05:46,936
[Hina] Going up against a team like that...
don't you need your fan club?

77
00:05:47,020 --> 00:05:48,730
My fan club, huh?

78
00:05:48,813 --> 00:05:52,901
And anyway, it'd be nice
to see the guy I like doing his best.

79
00:05:52,984 --> 00:05:55,904
Why'd you bring that up outta... Uh...

80
00:05:58,990 --> 00:06:01,659
You can't just turn around like that
all of a sudden!

81
00:06:01,743 --> 00:06:04,329
Someone's gonna get hurt
if you don't look where you're going!

82
00:06:04,412 --> 00:06:06,581
- Jeez! You big, dumb, stupid...
- Ow!

83
00:06:06,664 --> 00:06:09,250
- Okay, okay, I got it! Hey! Come on!
- [Hina whines]

84
00:06:14,506 --> 00:06:16,424
[panting]

85
00:06:16,508 --> 00:06:17,675
{\an8}EIMEI PRIVATE HIGH SCHOOL

86
00:06:17,759 --> 00:06:19,719
{\an8}- Good morning.
- Good morning.

87
00:06:22,138 --> 00:06:23,598
[racket swooshing]

88
00:06:38,113 --> 00:06:38,947
[grunts]

89
00:06:40,031 --> 00:06:41,241
[grunts]

90
00:06:42,534 --> 00:06:44,202
[pants]

91
00:06:45,703 --> 00:06:47,580
- [door opens]
- [exclaims softly]

92
00:06:47,664 --> 00:06:48,957
Oh, well, good morning.

93
00:06:50,041 --> 00:06:51,251
Morning.

94
00:06:51,334 --> 00:06:53,461
Wow, you're fired up today.

95
00:06:53,545 --> 00:06:56,047
I guess... kinda.

96
00:06:56,131 --> 00:06:57,966
You're getting ready
for the practice match?

97
00:06:58,049 --> 00:06:59,092
[Taiki] Hm?

98
00:06:59,843 --> 00:07:02,971
<i>This gym is a rumor mill.
Word really gets around.</i>

99
00:07:04,055 --> 00:07:05,223
Saturday, right?

100
00:07:06,182 --> 00:07:08,977
My practice ends at noon,
so I'll come see you after.

101
00:07:09,060 --> 00:07:10,645
- [Taiki] Huh?
- Hm?

102
00:07:10,728 --> 00:07:14,065
I mean, this isn't really the kind
of thing you need to come watch.

103
00:07:14,149 --> 00:07:15,483
But I think it's gonna be fun.

104
00:07:17,360 --> 00:07:19,988
It's not like it's an official match
or anything, so...

105
00:07:21,030 --> 00:07:23,283
It isn't really something
that's worth seeing.

106
00:07:23,366 --> 00:07:25,994
No way. Of course I wanna see it.

107
00:07:26,077 --> 00:07:27,495
[♪ peaceful music playing]

108
00:07:27,579 --> 00:07:30,832
[Hina] <i>It'd be nice to see
the guy I like doing his best.</i>

109
00:07:31,583 --> 00:07:32,709
[Taiki grunts softly]

110
00:07:32,792 --> 00:07:34,002
[Chinatsu] Hm?

111
00:07:34,085 --> 00:07:36,004
Oh, no, it's nothing.

112
00:07:36,880 --> 00:07:39,507
[Taiki] <i>It's only 'cause
Hina put that in my head.</i>

113
00:07:40,592 --> 00:07:43,428
Well, I guess I have no right to stop you.

114
00:07:43,511 --> 00:07:45,263
Uh-huh. So, I'll be there.

115
00:07:46,681 --> 00:07:50,268
I can't miss your epic gameplay,
Morning Practice Pal. [chuckles]

116
00:07:52,604 --> 00:07:53,771
[gasps softly]

117
00:07:59,110 --> 00:08:00,695
[racket whipping]

118
00:08:37,607 --> 00:08:39,692
Taiki! What have you been eating?

119
00:08:39,776 --> 00:08:41,110
You got even better, again!

120
00:08:41,945 --> 00:08:44,072
[Taiki] I haven't eaten
anything different.

121
00:08:45,532 --> 00:08:47,575
<i>I still have so much I need to work on.</i>

122
00:08:51,037 --> 00:08:52,747
<i>He was one step ahead of me.</i>

123
00:08:54,332 --> 00:08:56,084
<i>That's exactly how it felt.</i>

124
00:08:57,043 --> 00:08:58,211
[boy] Yo, did you hear?

125
00:08:58,294 --> 00:09:01,589
Yusa from Sajikawa beat one of the players
from the Japan Rusters.

126
00:09:02,465 --> 00:09:04,425
Wait, he beat a player at pro-level?

127
00:09:04,509 --> 00:09:06,094
He's still a first-year, right?

128
00:09:06,177 --> 00:09:07,720
[boy] He's a real beast.

129
00:09:11,516 --> 00:09:14,102
Tanigawa! Let's play another match!

130
00:09:14,185 --> 00:09:15,353
Again?

131
00:09:16,145 --> 00:09:17,105
[Nishida] Taiki...

132
00:09:17,772 --> 00:09:21,025
Consider playing against me, your captain.

133
00:09:21,109 --> 00:09:22,986
Oh, no, don't try and get outta this.

134
00:09:23,069 --> 00:09:25,363
- Loser has to plank for five minutes.
- [Nishida] Oh!

135
00:09:25,446 --> 00:09:28,575
But don't you think someone
should knock him down a peg or two

136
00:09:28,658 --> 00:09:30,618
since he's on a winning streak?

137
00:09:31,244 --> 00:09:32,537
I'm not sweatin' it.

138
00:09:32,620 --> 00:09:35,415
He doesn't seem pleased even when he wins.

139
00:09:35,498 --> 00:09:37,667
Even when people see you doing well,

140
00:09:37,750 --> 00:09:40,628
sometimes it's impossible
to accept that validation.

141
00:09:40,712 --> 00:09:41,921
[Nishida grunts]

142
00:09:42,005 --> 00:09:45,008
The thing is, he's been
practicing so hard, and getting better.

143
00:09:45,091 --> 00:09:47,135
I think he's pushing himself pretty hard

144
00:09:47,218 --> 00:09:49,137
'cause he wants to beat that Sajikawa kid.

145
00:09:49,887 --> 00:09:52,015
It's got to be tough
putting in all this hard work

146
00:09:52,098 --> 00:09:53,641
and feeling like you're not improving.

147
00:09:54,225 --> 00:09:56,561
Okay, sensei, then go
give him some advice.

148
00:09:56,644 --> 00:09:59,397
[Haryu] No, thanks.
I'm competing for one of the spots

149
00:09:59,480 --> 00:10:01,399
at nationals next year, too.

150
00:10:01,482 --> 00:10:04,777
I need my underclassmen
to struggle just a little bit.

151
00:10:05,820 --> 00:10:08,573
You're so immature. This calls for...

152
00:10:08,656 --> 00:10:10,908
- the captain to step--
- [Coach Yuasa] Nishida!

153
00:10:10,992 --> 00:10:12,285
[exclaims] Yes!

154
00:10:12,368 --> 00:10:14,287
Did you sign the club's
expenses application?

155
00:10:14,370 --> 00:10:17,290
Oh, I'm sorry about that, sir!
I was planning to do it later,

156
00:10:17,373 --> 00:10:20,418
but I got busy with stuff for
the Cultural Festival. I'm really sorry!

157
00:10:21,044 --> 00:10:23,421
[bell chiming]

158
00:10:29,802 --> 00:10:31,763
[♪ happy music playing]

159
00:10:37,226 --> 00:10:40,438
This apple is so glossy. It looks great!

160
00:10:40,521 --> 00:10:43,941
We got it at the hundred-yen shop,
and then Hina gave it a coat of paint.

161
00:10:44,025 --> 00:10:46,444
[girl 2] Something about it
"lacking luster."

162
00:10:47,904 --> 00:10:49,238
Actually, where is she?

163
00:10:49,322 --> 00:10:51,949
[girl 1] I think she's in the classroom
rehearsing lines.

164
00:10:52,575 --> 00:10:54,452
Oh, I see.

165
00:10:58,414 --> 00:11:01,459
Hina. Can I help you with anything?

166
00:11:01,542 --> 00:11:03,586
[♪ grandiose music playing]

167
00:11:05,171 --> 00:11:07,465
- She's dead!
- Nuh-uh.

168
00:11:08,091 --> 00:11:10,093
I was just practicing for the play!

169
00:11:10,176 --> 00:11:12,970
Oh, yeah, the last scene
where Snow White wakes up.

170
00:11:14,680 --> 00:11:18,351
It's the only scene where I don't know
how I'm supposed to look.

171
00:11:21,270 --> 00:11:22,855
I can help you rehearse.

172
00:11:22,939 --> 00:11:23,773
Huh?

173
00:11:24,440 --> 00:11:26,984
Wouldn't it be easier
with a scene partner?

174
00:11:27,610 --> 00:11:28,820
[Hina] It would be, but...

175
00:11:28,903 --> 00:11:29,987
SNOW WHITE SCRIPT

176
00:11:31,072 --> 00:11:32,240
THE PRINCE KISSES HER

177
00:11:32,865 --> 00:11:34,992
- Not doing that!
- Yeah, obviously!

178
00:11:39,580 --> 00:11:40,957
[Hina sighs]

179
00:11:41,040 --> 00:11:42,542
[clears throat]

180
00:11:42,625 --> 00:11:44,752
All righty, so what are you
having trouble with?

181
00:11:45,795 --> 00:11:47,004
How are you supposed to look

182
00:11:47,088 --> 00:11:49,090
when you're coming back
from the brink of death?

183
00:11:49,173 --> 00:11:50,758
That's trouble all right.

184
00:11:50,842 --> 00:11:53,136
And then, as if that wasn't enough,

185
00:11:53,219 --> 00:11:55,763
the queen tricked her
into eating a poison apple.

186
00:11:55,847 --> 00:11:59,142
If we look at it from the perspective
that Snow White knows that...

187
00:11:59,225 --> 00:12:01,811
[cackling]

188
00:12:01,894 --> 00:12:04,897
I am the fairest of them all!

189
00:12:06,399 --> 00:12:09,777
I'll never forgive you!
I shall have your head for this!

190
00:12:10,653 --> 00:12:12,238
Now bring me my sword!

191
00:12:12,905 --> 00:12:14,782
You're too bloodthirsty.

192
00:12:15,366 --> 00:12:19,036
I know! The prince is there when
she wakes up, so her heart skips a beat.

193
00:12:23,624 --> 00:12:25,168
{\an8}[Hina] Who the hell are you?

194
00:12:25,251 --> 00:12:27,044
{\an8}[Taiki] Now you're too suspicious.

195
00:12:29,172 --> 00:12:32,049
I know that.
This is not the way to play it.

196
00:12:32,800 --> 00:12:35,386
What do I do? This scene really matters.

197
00:12:36,095 --> 00:12:38,055
And I have to perform well at the end.

198
00:12:38,764 --> 00:12:40,558
{\an8}A near death experience...

199
00:12:41,309 --> 00:12:43,853
{\an8}is sorta like
surviving finals week, right?

200
00:12:44,562 --> 00:12:46,689
{\an8}- You're amazing, you know that, Hina?
- Huh?

201
00:12:46,772 --> 00:12:49,066
{\an8}You could be doing this
without thinking so hard,

202
00:12:49,775 --> 00:12:52,028
but instead, you're giving it your all.

203
00:12:52,111 --> 00:12:55,072
You've always got the script,
reading it over and over.

204
00:12:55,823 --> 00:12:58,075
If it were me,
I'd just look happy in this scene.

205
00:12:58,159 --> 00:13:01,120
When I take something on,
I really go for it.

206
00:13:01,871 --> 00:13:04,123
- Aren't you the same way?
- Huh?

207
00:13:06,250 --> 00:13:09,086
One second, you're in our classroom
helping with the play,

208
00:13:09,170 --> 00:13:12,089
then the next, you're back
in the gym for badminton practice.

209
00:13:12,173 --> 00:13:13,841
[laughs]

210
00:13:14,800 --> 00:13:17,345
You're also really amazing, Taiki.

211
00:13:17,428 --> 00:13:18,471
[grunts softly]

212
00:13:19,931 --> 00:13:21,015
[grunts softly]

213
00:13:22,934 --> 00:13:24,852
[Hina] You know, everyone was saying that!

214
00:13:25,978 --> 00:13:27,855
Anyway, let's get to rehearsing!

215
00:13:27,939 --> 00:13:30,650
Maybe we should just run the scene
and see how it goes.

216
00:13:31,234 --> 00:13:33,569
Then I'll start
from the line before yours.

217
00:13:33,653 --> 00:13:35,988
<i>I've been feeling overwhelmed lately,</i>

218
00:13:36,072 --> 00:13:38,866
<i>so I'm glad to hear
I've been doing my job well.</i>

219
00:13:39,534 --> 00:13:43,371
"Oh, Snow White,
I beg you, please wake up."

220
00:13:44,372 --> 00:13:45,540
There.

221
00:13:46,207 --> 00:13:47,917
You have been kissed.

222
00:14:00,346 --> 00:14:01,389
Hina?

223
00:14:03,015 --> 00:14:04,892
Is this part of your acting?

224
00:14:05,893 --> 00:14:07,019
I can't.

225
00:14:09,981 --> 00:14:12,483
I couldn't help
but imagine the real thing.

226
00:14:13,484 --> 00:14:15,403
{\an8}Kissing you for real, Taiki.

227
00:14:15,987 --> 00:14:17,405
What?

228
00:14:23,494 --> 00:14:25,454
[heartbeat thumping]

229
00:14:31,335 --> 00:14:32,795
Wanna do it for real?

230
00:14:32,879 --> 00:14:35,089
[heartbeat thumping continues]

231
00:14:35,172 --> 00:14:36,340
[Taiki gasps]

232
00:14:40,136 --> 00:14:41,637
[Hina] Wanna do it for real?

233
00:14:52,356 --> 00:14:53,441
No, I don't.

234
00:14:56,027 --> 00:14:58,070
[Hina] Well, I know that!

235
00:14:58,154 --> 00:15:00,948
If you'd said yes,
that would've been a turnoff!

236
00:15:03,534 --> 00:15:04,493
Although...

237
00:15:05,995 --> 00:15:07,872
your heart skipped a beat, didn't it?

238
00:15:09,832 --> 00:15:12,376
This is all part
of the great Hina's strategy!

239
00:15:14,670 --> 00:15:15,922
Well,

240
00:15:16,005 --> 00:15:18,466
I guess I'll go see
how everyone else is doing.

241
00:15:23,846 --> 00:15:25,014
[Taiki sighs]

242
00:15:35,316 --> 00:15:37,985
[groans]

243
00:15:38,069 --> 00:15:39,695
[Hina] <i>I like you.</i>

244
00:15:40,279 --> 00:15:41,530
A romantic way.

245
00:15:41,614 --> 00:15:45,993
That's fine, as long as it reminds you
that I have a crush on you, Taiki.

246
00:15:46,077 --> 00:15:47,244
[bangs on table]

247
00:15:48,496 --> 00:15:49,997
[groans]

248
00:15:51,123 --> 00:15:52,750
[exhales]

249
00:15:57,088 --> 00:15:58,506
[rackets swooshing]

250
00:16:00,883 --> 00:16:02,093
[sneakers screeching]

251
00:16:05,388 --> 00:16:07,390
- [grunts]
- [boy] Game, set, match.

252
00:16:07,473 --> 00:16:09,850
[Taiki pants]

253
00:16:13,396 --> 00:16:14,563
[Taiki] <i>Why?</i>

254
00:16:15,773 --> 00:16:17,191
<i>I can beat other people,</i>

255
00:16:17,274 --> 00:16:20,277
<i>and yet the gap between our scores
has only gotten wider.</i>

256
00:16:21,153 --> 00:16:23,739
<i>I can't believe
how much work I have to do.</i>

257
00:16:24,532 --> 00:16:26,075
<i>And at the very least,</i>

258
00:16:26,784 --> 00:16:28,577
<i>Yusa was better than this.</i>

259
00:16:31,539 --> 00:16:32,748
Hey, Taiki.

260
00:16:34,125 --> 00:16:36,293
Shots without confidence behind them...

261
00:16:37,044 --> 00:16:38,421
don't work on me.

262
00:16:39,171 --> 00:16:40,172
Duh.

263
00:16:40,756 --> 00:16:41,590
What?

264
00:16:43,884 --> 00:16:45,761
[Taiki] <i>As if I lack confidence.</i>

265
00:16:48,431 --> 00:16:50,433
[girls squealing excitedly]

266
00:16:50,516 --> 00:16:53,102
Miss Chono, superb as ever!

267
00:16:53,728 --> 00:16:55,855
<i>- I don't, but...</i>
- [Nagisa] Natsu!

268
00:16:57,314 --> 00:16:58,315
Nice!

269
00:17:05,781 --> 00:17:07,116
[Taiki] <i>I'm just pathetic.</i>

270
00:17:09,535 --> 00:17:11,620
[Nishida] What?

271
00:17:12,204 --> 00:17:14,623
Guys, Class D is having a curry tasting!

272
00:17:15,541 --> 00:17:17,209
[stomach rumbling]

273
00:17:18,544 --> 00:17:19,754
Let's go get some!

274
00:17:19,837 --> 00:17:21,130
Man, I hate curry.

275
00:17:21,213 --> 00:17:22,882
Does such a person exist?

276
00:17:23,716 --> 00:17:25,134
Curry, curry!

277
00:17:25,217 --> 00:17:27,720
I'll eat the curry! I'll drink the curry!

278
00:17:30,473 --> 00:17:31,557
[Haryu] Hey, Chii.

279
00:17:33,142 --> 00:17:34,310
Oh, hey, Haryu.

280
00:17:34,852 --> 00:17:36,479
You got night practice?

281
00:17:36,562 --> 00:17:37,897
Not tonight,

282
00:17:37,980 --> 00:17:40,399
but I had to stay
for the Cultural Festival stuff.

283
00:17:41,233 --> 00:17:44,653
Wow I'm impressed.
Since you're busy with practice, too.

284
00:17:45,362 --> 00:17:47,990
You really are self-disciplined, huh?

285
00:17:48,908 --> 00:17:50,659
No way, I'm not at all.

286
00:17:51,619 --> 00:17:53,537
You're the first person
at practice every day,

287
00:17:53,621 --> 00:17:56,165
that means in my book,
you are self-disciplined.

288
00:17:56,248 --> 00:17:57,500
[chuckles]

289
00:17:58,751 --> 00:18:00,461
Well Inomata, from your team,

290
00:18:00,544 --> 00:18:03,172
sometimes beats me to practice,
now that you mention it.

291
00:18:06,300 --> 00:18:10,012
I would say Taiki's more diligent
than self-disciplined.

292
00:18:10,638 --> 00:18:12,723
I hear that they have frankfurters, too!

293
00:18:12,807 --> 00:18:14,183
For real? Let's franken go!

294
00:18:15,226 --> 00:18:16,560
What's the difference?

295
00:18:16,644 --> 00:18:19,188
You're a sadist, and he's a masochist.

296
00:18:21,649 --> 00:18:23,734
You know when you wanna beat someone,

297
00:18:23,818 --> 00:18:25,569
and that's the goal that you set,

298
00:18:25,653 --> 00:18:27,696
you get focused
on all the things you can't do,

299
00:18:28,864 --> 00:18:31,325
and stop feeling good
about the things you can do.

300
00:18:33,994 --> 00:18:37,414
<i>But that's like wandering
through the desert without water.</i>

301
00:18:37,498 --> 00:18:38,791
<i>Why would you even do it?</i>

302
00:18:41,127 --> 00:18:43,879
Taiki is so focused on his shortcomings,

303
00:18:43,963 --> 00:18:45,965
that he forgets
to drink some water, you know?

304
00:18:47,341 --> 00:18:48,425
I get that.

305
00:18:49,218 --> 00:18:52,471
Him wanting so badly
just to hurry up and move forward.

306
00:18:54,640 --> 00:18:58,811
There are some people who drink
plenty of water, and they still give up.

307
00:19:00,062 --> 00:19:00,980
But...

308
00:19:02,106 --> 00:19:06,485
if you don't want to give up,
you just have to keep moving your legs.

309
00:19:07,820 --> 00:19:10,698
Because stopping
is what really torments you.

310
00:19:16,453 --> 00:19:18,289
I'd say you got a point.

311
00:19:20,207 --> 00:19:21,417
All righty then.

312
00:19:22,376 --> 00:19:23,961
I'm headed to night practice.

313
00:19:26,922 --> 00:19:27,840
Haryu.

314
00:19:29,091 --> 00:19:31,260
If you are that worried about him,

315
00:19:31,343 --> 00:19:34,013
offering him some water
might not be a bad thing.

316
00:19:35,306 --> 00:19:38,517
Besides, you are
an upperclassman after all.

317
00:19:40,352 --> 00:19:42,354
You know, I could use some water myself.

318
00:20:17,139 --> 00:20:18,766
[coins jingling]

319
00:20:21,644 --> 00:20:23,562
{\an8}- [beeps]
- [clattering]

320
00:20:30,277 --> 00:20:32,071
Hey, uh, Taiki...

321
00:20:32,696 --> 00:20:33,572
Yes?

322
00:20:33,656 --> 00:20:34,740
[grunts]

323
00:20:35,407 --> 00:20:37,076
You're eating curry right now?

324
00:20:38,535 --> 00:20:40,120
It's from Captain Nishida.

325
00:20:40,663 --> 00:20:42,331
[Haryu] Him, of all people...

326
00:20:42,414 --> 00:20:44,166
He's a nice captain, isn't he?

327
00:20:45,167 --> 00:20:47,211
I was planning on practicing with you,

328
00:20:47,294 --> 00:20:48,587
guess I'll ask Kyo.

329
00:20:49,463 --> 00:20:51,173
[Taiki] Wait, hold on!

330
00:20:52,675 --> 00:20:55,177
Oh. Could I have that water?

331
00:20:55,261 --> 00:20:56,720
The curry was spicy.

332
00:20:56,804 --> 00:20:59,306
- [Haryu] As if!
- [Taiki] Why not, though! Come on!

333
00:21:04,895 --> 00:21:06,105
[boy 1] Where are the birdies?

334
00:21:06,939 --> 00:21:08,315
[boy 2] Got 'em right here.

335
00:21:09,024 --> 00:21:10,609
[Nishida] Someone go get coach!

336
00:21:11,777 --> 00:21:13,320
I'll go and find him!

337
00:21:15,197 --> 00:21:17,074
[Taiki] <i>This current version of me...</i>

338
00:21:18,117 --> 00:21:19,368
<i>is pathetic.</i>

339
00:21:20,703 --> 00:21:23,330
<i>Hina confessed her feelings to me,</i>

340
00:21:23,414 --> 00:21:26,125
<i>and said she didn't need an answer back,</i>

341
00:21:26,208 --> 00:21:28,627
<i>but now I have no idea
how to move forward.</i>

342
00:21:30,462 --> 00:21:32,381
<i>And as an athlete...</i>

343
00:21:33,966 --> 00:21:35,342
<i>I'm the only one...</i>

344
00:21:36,302 --> 00:21:38,304
[♪ emotional music playing]

345
00:21:41,181 --> 00:21:43,142
<i>not making any progress.</i>

346
00:21:46,061 --> 00:21:47,146
<i>That's why...</i>

347
00:21:47,980 --> 00:21:49,398
[guy] Excuse me.

348
00:21:51,525 --> 00:21:52,401
[gasps softly]

349
00:21:58,407 --> 00:22:00,409
{\an8}Could you point me to where the gym is?

350
00:22:02,202 --> 00:22:03,287
[Taiki] <i>At least.</i>

351
00:22:05,497 --> 00:22:07,499
[closing theme song playing]
